<title>POLAND: EU car makers use up Polish import quota -ministry.</title>
<headline>EU car makers use up Polish import quota -ministry.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish importers have already fully used this year's 38,750-unit duty-free import quota for European Union-made passenger cars, the Economy Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said in a statement late on Thursday Fiat Spa Polish unit won the highest share of the quota by importing 4,624 Fiat, Alfa Romeo and Lancia cars.</p>
<p>The official dealer for Volkswagen, Audi and Porsche came second with 3,266 units imported and Spain's SEAT came third with 3,200 units.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
